AUDIO: 'below. Also this week, another open-source way to speed up MiniMax H3, the world\'s best open-source video model, has emerged, potentially making it faster than real-time. It\'s called Video Delta Net, and it\'s an attempt to make'

[06:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'MiniMax significantly faster without compromising video quality. You see, the problem here is the attention mechanism. In the full MiniMax H3, attention accounts for about 85% of the model\'s operating time. But Video DeltaNet'

[06:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'replaces it with a hybrid system. Simply put, neighboring frames still use expensive but accurate attention data, since fine details and motion are important there, and'

[06:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'information from distant frames is processed using much cheaper linear attention. Think of it as spending expensive computing resources on what\'s close and using compressed memory for everything that\'s far away. And when'

[06:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'combined with other optimization techniques , such as optimized kernels, parallelism, and eight-step distillation, you get a super-fast model with minimal loss of quality. As you can see from these'

